From c23cc2627d520704fbeeffd11d5f408f2f3cd34e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rick Yazwinski <rickyaz@meta.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 08:21:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/ssi/aspeed_smc: don't bus-fault on flash window access in
 read mode

Commit 80c5be9458 ("hw/ssi/aspeed_smc: Convert mem ops to
read/write_with_attrs for error handling") made aspeed_smc_flash_read()
and aspeed_smc_flash_write() return MEMTX_ERROR from their default
(unhandled command mode) switch arms instead of silently ignoring the
access as before.

On AST2500, U-Boot performs a stray write into the flash AHB window
while the controller is still in fast-read mode (CTRL_FREADMODE) during
recovery boot. Real Aspeed hardware ignores such an access; it does not
raise a bus error. Returning MEMTX_ERROR data-aborts the guest, which
breaks AST2500 SPL/U-Boot boot -- the board spins in a "Booting
recovery U-Boot." loop and never reaches Linux.

Restore the pre-regression behaviour: log the unexpected mode but treat
the access as a no-op (read returns zeroed data) and return MEMTX_OK.
Genuine error propagation for the unwritable-flash case is preserved.

Reproduced with: qemu-system-aarch64 -machine tiogapass-bmc on a signed
fbtp (AST2500) image; boots to Linux with this change, loops without it.
---
 hw/ssi/aspeed_smc.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/ssi/aspeed_smc.c b/hw/ssi/aspeed_smc.c
index bf596f7b2d..b616e614a8 100644
--- a/hw/ssi/aspeed_smc.c
+++ b/hw/ssi/aspeed_smc.c
@@ -534,8 +534,15 @@ static MemTxResult aspeed_smc_flash_read(void *opaque, hwaddr addr,
         aspeed_smc_flash_unselect(fl);
         break;
     default:
+        /*
+         * A read from the flash AHB window while the controller is in an
+         * unexpected command mode is ignored by real Aspeed hardware -- it
+         * does not raise a bus error. Returning MEMTX_ERROR here data-aborts
+         * the guest and breaks AST2500 SPL/U-Boot boot (recovery loop), so
+         * keep the legacy behaviour: return zeroed data with MEMTX_OK.
+         */
         aspeed_smc_error("invalid flash mode %d", aspeed_smc_flash_mode(fl));
-        return MEMTX_ERROR;
+        break;
     }
 
     trace_aspeed_smc_flash_read(fl->cs, addr, size, *data,
@@ -575,8 +582,15 @@ static MemTxResult aspeed_smc_flash_write(void *opaque, hwaddr addr,
         aspeed_smc_flash_unselect(fl);
         break;
     default:
+        /*
+         * A write to the flash AHB window while the controller is in a read
+         * command mode (e.g. fast-read) is ignored by real Aspeed hardware --
+         * it does not raise a bus error. AST2500 U-Boot performs such a stray
+         * write during recovery boot; returning MEMTX_ERROR data-aborts the
+         * guest and breaks the boot (recovery loop). Ignore it with MEMTX_OK.
+         */
         aspeed_smc_error("invalid flash mode %d", aspeed_smc_flash_mode(fl));
-        return MEMTX_ERROR;
+        break;
     }
 
     return MEMTX_OK;
